Article 23 Education for persons with disabilities shall be provided in accordance with the following requirements based on their physical and mental characteristics and needs:
(1) While conducting ideological and cultural education, strengthen physical and mental compensation and vocational education;
(2) Adopt ordinary education methods or special education methods based on the type of disability and receptivity;
(3) The curriculum setting, teaching materials, teaching methods, age of enrollment and at school in special education may have moderate flexibility.

Article 43 The government and society shall adopt the following measures to enrich the spiritual and cultural life of persons with disabilities:
(1) Publicize and report on the work and life of persons with disabilities in a timely manner through radio, film, television, newspapers, books, the Internet and other forms, and serve persons with disabilities;
(2) Organize and support the compilation and publication of Braille books, audiobooks for the blind and other reading materials for persons with disabilities, and, based on the actual needs of the blind, set up Braille books and audiobooks for the blind reading rooms in public libraries;
(3) Launch sign language television programs, launch special radio columns for persons with disabilities, and promote the addition of subtitles and dubbing to television programs and film and television productions;
(4) Organize and support persons with disabilities to carry out mass cultural, sports and recreational activities, hold special art performances and sports meets for persons with disabilities, and participate in international competitions and exchanges;
(5) Provide convenience and care for persons with disabilities at cultural, sports, recreational and other public activity venues. Build activity venues for persons with disabilities in a planned manner.
